  a device with no intended configuration is the one case where a DeployWorkflow can push
  nothing and still report COMPLETED, so deploying it would manufacture a false success —
  and this failure is not one a deploy can fix. It is a platform fault, most often the
  location-resolver plugin, which 500s for EVERY device at once rather than one
  (challenges/nvcm_render_location_hierarchy_bug.md). Fix that, then re-run: this door is
  safe to re-run: every stage is idempotent and an already-configured device just
  produces an empty diff. It does NOT skip them, though — a re-run is a full pass over
  every device you pass, so budget the same time.
